WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.860
The version of Captain Marvel that hit theaters
was clipped-down and polished-up, missing

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:07.740
a handful of scenes you'll wish you got to
see on a 50-foot screen.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.960
Here's a look at all the scenes that didn't
make it to theaters.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:16.380
While she's living on Hala and going by "Vers,"
Carol pays the Supreme Intelligence a visit

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:21.760
and sees it as Mar-Vell, aka Dr. Wendy Lawson,
the Kree scientist with whom Carol worked

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:22.940
in the U.S. Air Force.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.420
Yon-Rogg accompanies her to the meeting, but
the finished film doesn't show him having

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.460
his own encounter with the A.I. overlord.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:34.370
Since the Supreme Intelligence appears to
its guest as the person they most admire,

00:00:34.370 --> 00:00:38.480
when Yon-Rogg meets with it, he naturally
sees the spitting image of himself.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.940
"We both know your admiration is mostly reserved
for yourself."

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:47.640
The Supreme Intelligence chastises Yon-Rogg
for the failures of his mission six years

00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:52.460
prior, from killing Mar-Vell to not retrieving
the energy core she built, and leaving Carol

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.540
alive as a supercharged liability.

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:59.200
The usually cocky Yon-Rogg is shaken, and
begs the Supreme Intelligence to allow him

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:03.900
to kill Carol to make up for his mistakes
a proposition the A.I. denies.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:13.020
"Bring us the core and the girl — alive,
Yon-Rogg."

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:17.480
Of all the film's deleted scenes, this is
the one that co-directors Anna Boden and Ryan

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:20.120
Fleck have said they wished made it to theaters
the most.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.299
Speaking to CinemaBlend, Boden said,

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:26.479
"I think the scene where Jude visits his Supreme
Intelligence is really fun [...] Jude Law

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:31.100
is playing both characters and being both
brutal and vulnerable in the same space."

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:36.300
One deleted sequence features Yon-Rogg lecturing
a group of young Starforce hopefuls about

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:40.060
the Kree Empire's mission to protect itself
from the shapeshifting Skrulls.

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:45.000
Yon-Rogg teases the recruits about potentially
being shapeshifters themselves before turning

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.200
his attention to Vers, calling her the best
example of Kree potential.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:52.499
Vers then enters the room and shares her own
disdain for the Skrulls.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.520
"The commander's right about the Skrulls.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.160
They took everything from me.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:56.940
My home.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:58.400
My family.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:01:59.820
My memory."

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:04.840
She also calls attention to the implant in
her neck, which she still wholeheartedly believes

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:07.539
is a good thing, and the source of her powers.

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:13.020
"Our leader the Supreme Intelligence saved
me, gave me purpose, and this implant, so

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:16.440
I can fight back."

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:22.400
Early on in Captain Marvel, the members of
Starforce fly to Torfa, a planet on the border

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:26.460
of the Kree Empire, to locate and rescue the
missing Kree spy Soh-Larr.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:31.000
The expedition ends up a total failure when
the Skrulls successfully snatch up Vers as

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:32.040
part of a trap.

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:36.380
Before things go south, the movie was meant
to include some light-hearted banter to send

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.760
the Starforce gang off on a happy note.

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:43.410
One deleted scene shows Vers joking around
with Minn-Erva, Korath, and Att-Lass, who

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:47.180
tease her about a previous mission to which
she brought a little too much heat with her

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:48.800
Photon-blasting fists.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:52.440
"That was not my fault, we were specifically
told to bring the heat."

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.340
"It was very hot."

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:58.700
Minn-Erva, calling her by the name of "Twinkle
Fists," gives her a sarcastic piece of advice:

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:00.820
think with your head, not your hands.

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:06.220
The fun momentarily stops when Yon-Rogg arrives
and reminds them of the task at hand: bring

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.320
Soh-Larr home to Hala safely.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:13.150
Bron-Char manages to sneak in one last quip
as the Starforce team is loading into their

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:14.220
containment vessels:

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.460
"Does anyone else get claustrophobic in these
things?"

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:23.020
In an extended version of Carol's interaction
with the man on the motorcycle, things get

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:25.780
kicked up a notch after he asks her for a
smile.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:30.180
First of all, we learn that Vers isn't the
only character in the scene with a weird name.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:31.760
"I'm Vers."

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.480
"People call me The Don."

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:38.340
Instead of a grin, Carol asks if he's up for
a handshake.

00:03:38.349 --> 00:03:42.959
He obliges but she uses her fiery fists to
burn his hand, leaving him helpless in her

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:43.959
alien grip.

00:03:44.060 --> 00:03:45.520
"Here's a proposition for you.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:49.600
You're going to give me your jacket, your
helmet, and your motorcycle, and in return

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.800
I'm going to let you keep your hand."

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:56.140
The scene may have been cut for making our
heroine appear a little bit too much like

00:03:56.150 --> 00:04:00.250
Marvel's own Terminator which may have been
an intentional reference, considering the

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:01.360
shared ‘90s setting.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:06.670
As the now-in-pain Don hands Carol his keys,
she places a sassy cherry on top of their

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:07.360
conversation:

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:08.660
"What, no smile?"

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:13.060
Ben Mendelsohn gives a chameleonic performance
as Skrull leader Talos.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:17.560
While audiences still think Talos is a villain,
he shape-shifts to disguise himself as Keller,

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:19.300
the ‘90s-era Director of S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:23.080
What follows is a cat-and-mouse game between
Talos, Carol, and Nick Fury.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:26.820
One scene that got snipped from this plot
shows Keller attempting to track down the

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:29.860
Quadjet Carol and Nick stole from the Air
Force Academy.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:35.600
"So you're telling me you can't track your
own plane."

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:40.120
Since the plane has anti-radar tech, there's
no way for Talos to immediately locate it

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:44.440
— which means he's further away from discovering
the truth about Carol, Wendy Lawson, and the

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:45.780
location of his family.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:46.900
But when another S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:52.060
agent hands Talos some intel on the crash
site and Maria Lambeau, his chances of cracking

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:54.420
the whole thing wide open greatly improve.

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:59.240
Speaking of Talos, another Captain Marvel
scene you didn't get to see reveals what happened

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:02.820
to the real S.H.I.E.L.D. director after the
green-skinned Skrull stole his look.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:08.020
It would have played out right after Talos-as-Keller
says goodbye to his fallen Skrull comrade,

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:11.000
the one who Nick Fury killed while he was
impersonating Phil Coulson.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:15.479
Things end there in the theatrical cut, but
the deleted scene keeps going, making sure

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:18.680
it's clear to everybody that there's some
shapeshifting going on.

00:05:18.820 --> 00:05:22.819
Out in the hallway, the true Agent Coulson
passes by Nick Fury, and offers to be his

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:24.820
partner in the ongoing investigation.

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.060
Fury rejects him.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:28.220
"Here's that police report you're after.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:28.720
Need a partner?"

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:30.080
"Not now, rook."

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:34.410
Trying to prove himself useful, Coulson jumps
at the chance to help Keller get into his

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:38.570
office — not knowing it's actually Talos,
who forgot to grab Keller's I.D. card when

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:39.800
he first took his form.

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:41.160
Who's the rookie now?

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:45.360
Coulson happily swipes his key card through
the scanner on the wall, granting Talos access

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:46.860
to the real Keller's office.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:50.729
There, we see the S.H.I.E.L.D. director on
the floor, bound and unconscious, and watch

00:05:50.729 --> 00:05:53.800
as Talos grabs Keller's badge from underneath
his jacket.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.920
Unlike some of the other sequences, it makes
sense why this scene was cut.

00:05:58.070 --> 00:06:01.760
The only people it would play as a reveal
to would be viewers just getting back from

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:02.380
the bathroom.

